Platform Purpose - Box AI functions as an intelligent content management enhancement that integrates advanced AI models directly into your secure cloud storage to streamline how you interact with business files. By leveraging this tool, you can perform Natural Language queries across individual or multiple documents to find specific details, such as contract clauses or financial figures, without manually scanning through large volumes of text. Box AI turns your content into an intelligent knowledge base you can query naturally, eliminating the need for tedious manual document reviews and enabling teams to find answers in seconds instead of hours. Box AI's core capabilities span content insights, intelligent automation, and secure, customizable agents designed for enterprise workflows such as Automated data extraction, Instant Document Analysis and Q&A and Permissions-Aware Security. Box AI is built for enterprise teams across nearly every department and industry—from financial services and legal to marketing, sales, and operations—where content-heavy workflows and compliance requirements are paramount.
Intended Use Case - Box AI is designed to embed intelligent agents throughout your organization's content workflows, transforming unstructured data into actionable insights while maintaining enterprise security. The platform uses AI agents to automate complex, multi-step work and integrates with your existing systems, leveraging models from OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, and other providers to match each task's demands. Content Generation = Context-aware content tailored to your audience. Software Development Assistance = Custom fields and instructions your teams define. Knowledge Search = Context-aware information retrieval across complex files. Data Analytics = AI agents that extract and interpret unstructured data. Workflow Automation = Agentic automation with conditional branching and routing.
Prohibited Use Case(s) - Box AI should not be used for uploading regulated data without proper approval, processing customer personally identifiable information without authorization, making fully autonomous decisions, or sharing confidential information with unauthorized users. Each use case carries distinct compliance and security risks that organizations must actively prevent. Uploading Regulated Data Without Approval (Compliance Risk) = Data may breach industry regulations; customer responsibility to ensure legal compliance before use. Processing Customer PII Without Authorization (Privacy/Consent Risk) = Unauthorized processing violates data protection laws; strict adherence to permissions is required. Fully Autonomous Decision Making (Governance Risk) = AI outputs lack human oversight for high-risk decisions; inherent limitations mean AI should not drive consequential outcomes alone. Sharing Confidential Information with Unauthorized Users (Security Risk) = Strict controls and permissions prevent data leakage; unauthorized sharing violates access policies.
Data Considerations - Box AI enforces strict data governance to ensure enterprise information stays protected while enabling responsible AI use. Data governance for AI requires clear permission rules, privacy policies, and audit trails—Box implements these through classification, access controls, and retention management across your content. Data Access: What's Permitted = AI sees only what users can access (permission-aligned). What's Restricted = Unauthorized access; external sharing. Key Controls for Data Access = Strict adherence to permissions matching user roles. Classified Data: What's Permitted = Public, Internal, Restricted, Restricted–Collaborative categories. What's Restricted = Unclassified or misclassified sensitive data. Key Controls for Classified Data = Automatic classification of PII as Restricted. Regulated Data: What's Permitted = HIPAA, GDPR, SEC/FINRA, FedRAMP High compliant use. What's Restricted = Use without governance; non-compliant workflows. Key Controls for Regulated Data = Governance for data handling, auditing, and retention. Prohibited Usage: What's Permitted = Insight, classification, document Q&A. What's Restricted = Spam, privacy violations, protected-class decisions. Key Controls for Prohibited Usage = Safety filters; user transparency. Retention: What's Permitted = Modifiable retention policies; legal holds. What's Restricted = Premature deletion; untracked data lifecycle. Key Controls for Retention = Box Governance retention policies with e-discovery integration.
Key Risks - Leakage or Unathorized Data Access = AI logs and model inputs/outputs may contain sensitive enterprise data; unauthorized access or inadvertent exposure during training or storage. Excessive Data Collection Beyond Necessity = Box AI systems may collect, retain, or transmit more customer data than strictly necessary for the intended AI function, violating data minimization principles. Inadequate Audit Trail & Documentation for Regulatory Investigations. Box AI may lack sufficient logging, audit trails, and documentation of AI decision-making, data usage, and compliance controls, making it difficult to demonstrate compliance during regulatory investigations or litigation. Vendor Non-Compliance with Security & Privacy Standards = AI service providers may fail to meet contractual security, data protection, or audit requirements; non-compliance may go undetected if monitoring is inadequate, cascading compliance failures to Box. Inadequate Access Controls and Privilege = Users may have access to more data than required for their role; inadequate access controls allow unauthorized data access, and insufficient monitoring enables privilege escalation attacks. Undefined Oversight Responsibilities & Authority Gaps = Organizational roles and responsibilities for Box AI oversight may be unclear; ownership of oversight decisions, accountability for failures, and escalation authority remain ambiguous. Monitoring & Alerting Gaps = Operational issues may not be detected promptly due to inadequate monitoring, alerting infrastructure, or alert fatigue; delayed detection extends incident duration and impact. 
